<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- A readable rumour that hands the player "The Claim" on the spot.

     WHY THIS EXISTS, and it is a load-budget decision before it is a fiction one.
     Jawa_TheClaim is root-selected (rootSelectionWeight 1.0) and therefore fires
     on the storyteller's own cadence. V1_SCOPE.md's gate is "seen working
     in-game ONCE" — and a cold load is ~23-30 minutes, so "wait for the
     storyteller" is the most expensive possible way to clear it. This item makes
     the quest fire ON DEMAND from a dev-spawned object, in seconds, without dev
     mode's quest generator and without touching the quest def.

     THE PATTERN IS BORROWED, NOT INVENTED. Space Tower's ST_TowerMap does
     exactly this (read during C2 due diligence): a tradeable item whose three
     comps give a quest and delete itself. Every class here is in the base
     assembly, verified against a SHIPPING def rather than a name that sounded
     right:

       ParentName ResourceBase              Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Base.xml L4
       CompProperties_Usable                Biotech/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Various.xml L144
       CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf  same file, L152
       CompProperties_UseEffectGiveQuest    same file, L153
       JobDef UseItem                       Core/Defs/JobDefs/Jobs_Misc.xml L461
       ThingCategoryDef ItemsMisc           Core/Defs/ThingCategoryDefs/ThingCategories.xml L259

     ⚠️ Those comps are USED by Biotech defs but the classes live in
     Assembly-CSharp, so this needs no DLC. Nothing here references a Biotech def.

     ⚠️ SCOPE — RULED by VISION 2026-08-13, and v1 is still only the object.
     Spec: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/v1_quest_the_claim.md, "The rumour item".

     The label is "salvage rumour", which is VISION's wording: the clan does not
     only trade in salvage, it trades in KNOWING WHERE THE SALVAGE IS. Two supply
     lanes are ruled, and BOTH are required:

       BOUGHT  primarily from the Hutt Cartel — they are the faction that knows
               where everything fell and will sell you anything, including your
               own location. The fast lane: you can buy your next opportunity.
       FOUND   wreck loot, raider inventories, ancient sites. Costs nothing but
               the risk already taken.

     ⛔ Purchase-only is explicitly forbidden. A clan that cannot afford rumours
     would simply stop receiving content, and that failure looks like the GAME
     being empty rather than the player being broke.

     🔴 NEITHER LANE IS IMPLEMENTED HERE, AND THAT IS CORRECT. v1 ships the bare
     object: it exists, it is dev-spawnable, reading it fires The Claim. Hutt
     trader stock and wreck loot tables are v2 — one line each, and the fiction
     is already written so that step is a stock entry rather than a redesign.
     Hence tradeability None, no faction, no cost, no Heat today. C2's later hook
     (buying a map from the Hutts puts you on the Empire's radar) also lands on
     this def when it lands, and the quest does not change either time.

     Dev route: Debug actions -> Spawn thing -> Jawa_ClaimRumour, then select a
     colonist and right-click it to read. -->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <!-- defName stays Jawa_ClaimRumour deliberately: a defName is never shown to
         the player, and renaming it would churn the quest reference and every
         save that holds one, for zero player-facing gain. The label/defName
         mismatch is intentional, not an oversight. -->
    <defName>Jawa_ClaimRumour</defName>
    <label>salvage rumour</label>
    <description>A scraped hide chart, rolled around a stub of iron cut for driving into wreckage. Somebody walked out far enough to see where the thing came down, and then walked back to sell what they saw.\n\nReading it tells you where to go. It does not tell you who else was told.</description>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/JawaClaimRumour</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <category>Item</category>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ItemsMisc</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>0.2</Mass>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>120</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Usable">
        <useJob>UseItem</useJob>
        <useLabel>Read the rumour</useLabel>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_UseEffectGiveQuest">
        <quest>Jawa_TheClaim</quest>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
